      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A clean categorisation derived from short_description, giving a strong grouping axis for explaining duration variation. Values match source text well (WiFi->network_connectivity, VPN->vpn_access, database->database)."
    },
    {
      "name": "failure_mode",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.8,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Adds a distinct axis (nature of failure) beyond category, useful for modelling duration. Mostly warranted (connect->connectivity_failure), though 'access online database'->access_denied is a plausible but slightly inferential reading."
    },
    {
      "name": "affected_system_scope",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.8,
      "source_groundedness": 0.75,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Server/network/client scope is a genuinely useful grouping for duration analysis. Values are reasonable inferences but sometimes soft (database->server_side, printing->client_side are plausible readings of terse text)."
    },
    {
      "name": "assigned_resolver",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.3,
      "source_groundedness": 0.95,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Values are a direct copy of the existing closed_by/assigned_to fields; well grounded but largely redundant with original columns, adding little new analytical leverage."
    },
    {
      "name": "resolver_match",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.55,
      "source_groundedness": 0.7,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A boolean of whether assignee equals closer could relate to duration, so it has some leverage. Derivable from original assigned_to vs closed_by, but samples only show closed_by, so the match basis is only partially verifiable."
    },
    {
      "name": "ticket_open_hour_band",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.7,
      "source_groundedness": 0.95,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Time-of-day band is a plausible driver of resolution duration (staffing shifts) and is cleanly derived from opened_at timestamps. Samples all correct."
    },
    {
      "name": "caller_id_group",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.25,
      "source_groundedness": 0.2,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Purports to group callers but the sampled values do not correspond to the source caller and appear unrelated/invented (source rows don't even show caller_id yet specific names are assigned). Redundant with caller_id and poorly grounded."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.62,
  "source_groundedness": 0.72,
  "rationale": "The semantic categorisation columns (incident_category, failure_mode, affected_system_scope) and ticket_open_hour_band provide genuine, well-grounded axes for explaining why resolution durations vary. assigned_resolver largely duplicates existing fields, resolver_match is partially verifiable, and caller_id_group appears both redundant and ungrounded (values not supported by the source). Overall the set offers real analytical leverage but with one clearly hallucinated column dragging groundedness down."
}
